##EBOOK DESIGN AND PACKAGING
Once your ebook content is complete, the next step is to turn your manuscript into a professionally designed PDF. A well-organised and visually appealing ebook improves readability and makes your product look more valuable to potential buyers.



Set Up Canva - 
Open Canva.
Create a free account or log in.
Search for Ebook or Ebook (Multiple Pages) in the templates section.
Browse the available designs and select a template that suits your niche.
Choose a clean and readable layout rather than an overly complicated design.



Design the Cover Page - 
Your cover is the first thing potential buyers see, so make it attractive and easy to understand.

Include:
Ebook title.
A short, descriptive subtitle.
Author name or brand name.
Relevant graphics or illustrations.

Keep the design simple, professional and consistent with your niche.



Organise the Ebook Pages - 
Use a consistent layout throughout the ebook.

Recommended page structure:
Cover Page
Copyright and Disclaimer Page (where applicable)
Table of Contents
Introduction
Main Chapters
Practical Examples, Charts and Checklists
Conclusion
Additional Resources or References (if applicable)



Add Visual Elements - 
Make the ebook easier to read by including relevant visual elements.

Use headings and subheadings to organise information.
Add charts, diagrams and illustrations wherever useful.
Highlight important information using callout boxes.
Include screenshots or examples where relevant and properly sourced.
Use consistent fonts, colours and spacing.
Avoid overcrowding pages with too much text.



Export Your Ebook - 

Once the design is complete:
Review every page for formatting issues.
Check spelling, alignment, page numbering and image quality.
Make sure all text is readable on mobile devices.
Click Share → Download in Canva.
Select PDF Standard for a lightweight digital ebook.
Download and open the PDF to verify that everything displays correctly.



Useful tool - 
Canva – Ebook templates, page layouts, cover designs and PDF export.
